{"title":"Mexico estimates of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/927534777/0/marginalrevolution~Mexico-estimates-of-the-day.html","date":1762927590000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Ms Sheinbaum’s government says Mexico’s murder rate has come down by 32% in the year since she took office. Analysis by <i>The Economist</i> confirms that the rate has fallen, though by a significantly smaller margin, 14%. Counting homicides alone misses an important part of the picture, namely the thousands of people who disappear in Mexico every year, many of whom are killed and buried in unmarked graves. A broader view of deadly crime that includes manslaughter, femicide and two-thirds of disappearances (the data for disappearances is imperfect), shows a more modest decline of 6% (see chart). Still, Mexico is on track for about 24,300 murders this year, horribly high, but well below the recent annual average of slightly over 30,000. Ms Sheinbaum is the first Mexican leader in years to push violent crime in the right direction.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.economist.com/the-americas/2025/11/10/mexico-has-become-a-less-deadly-place-under-claudia-sheinbaum?utm_campaign=shared_article\" target=\"_blank\">more from The Economist</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/mexico-estimates-of-the-day.html\">Mexico estimates of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/927534777/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/927534777/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/927534777/margina